    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "## Problem\n\nDescribe the problem (concisely).\n\n## Steps to reproduce\n\n```lua\nlocal api = vim.api\n\nvim.cmd.tabnew()\nvim.cmd.tabnew()\n\nlocal tab = api.nvim_get_current_tabpage()\nvim.cmd(\"split\")\n\nlocal group = api.nvim_create_augroup(\"test\")\nlocal on_close = function()\n\tif api.nvim_tabpage_is_valid(tab) then\n\t\tvim.cmd.tabclose({ bang = true, args = { api.nvim_tabpage_get_number(tab) } })\n\tend\nend\n\napi.nvim_create_autocmd(\"WinClosed\", { group = group, callback = on_close })\nvim.cmd.tabclose()\n\n```\n\n## Expected behavior\ntwo tabpage remain. actual: one tab remain.\n\n## System info\n\n- Nvim version (nvim -v): `v0.13.0-dev-1119 g09d5fd2d34` neovim/neovim@09d5fd2d34\n- Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?: ?\n- Operating system/version: Linux 7.1.4-zen1-1-zen\n- Terminal name/version: kitty\n- $TERM environment variable: `xterm-kitty`\n- Installation: ?\n\n",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
